# Project Context

Paradigm is a Windows desktop app built with Tauri v2. This worktree (`src/`)
is the frontend: React + TypeScript, built with Vite. The Rust backend lives
in a separate worktree, not visible here.

## Frontend stack
- UI components: shadcn/ui
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (core utility classes)
- Data fetching / state: TanStack Query
- The app uses multiple native Tauri windows, not a single-window SPA

## Talking to the backend
- All backend calls go through Tauri's `invoke()` from `@tauri-apps/api/core`
- Never invent a command name or signature — backend commands are built and
  communicated as they're ready (contract-triggered merge cadence, not a
  fixed schedule). If a command you need doesn't exist yet, flag it rather
  than guessing its shape.
- Two data tables the frontend reads/displays: `contacts_cache` (Chat Mode's
  email/contact resolution) and `profile_fields` / `form_field_mappings`
  (Form Memory's dropdown fuzzy-matching)

## AI model stack (context only — frontend never calls these directly)
- Local: Qwen2.5-0.5B (Ghost Mode labeling), Qwen3.5-0.8B-Vision (fallback)
- Cloud via Fireworks AI: Qwen3-7B-Instruct (intent/form Q&A), Qwen2-VL-7B
  (heavy vision/OCR)
Useful for building appropriate loading states — cloud calls are slower and
cost real money; local calls are near-instant and free.

## Shared components
Automation Preview is a single shared confirmation component used across
Ghost Mode, Chat Mode, and Form Memory, with feature-specific variants
(first-run, failure-state/drift-repair, vision-fallback, kill-switch-disabled).
Build it once as a reusable component — don't duplicate per feature.